<% meta('title', 'Privacy'); meta('description', 'How PocketCon handles your data.') %>
<section class="page prose">
  <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Short version: we keep what you need to attend and nothing we'd sell. Last updated November 14, 2026.</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    PocketCon 2027 is run by Ben Allfree and sponsored by PocketHost. Questions or requests:
    <a href="mailto:ben@pockethost.io">ben@pockethost.io</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Your account:</b> your email address and a password (stored hashed), or, if you sign in with Google or
      GitHub, your email address and the name and profile picture that service shares. We never see your Google or
      GitHub password.</li>
    <li><b>Talk proposals:</b> what you put in the form: your name, contact email, talk details, bio and links.
      Only the PocketCon team sees them.</li>
    <li><b>Basic server logs:</b> IP address, browser and the pages requested, kept for a short time to run and
      protect the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't take payments here and don't store payment or shipping details.</p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send you the stream link, schedule and PocketCon updates.</li>
    <li>To review talk proposals and contact speakers.</li>
    <li>To show attendee offers to registered people.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell your data or share it with advertisers.</p>

  <h2>Other services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The site runs on <a href="https://pockethost.io">PocketHost</a> behind Cloudflare.</li>
    <li>Fonts load from Google Fonts and a small script library from jsDelivr, so those services see your IP address.</li>
    <li>Sign-in with Google or GitHub goes through those companies under their own privacy policies.</li>
    <li>Attendee offers link to other sites (such as a merch store or PocketHost). What you do there is covered by
      their policies, not this one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>No tracking or advertising cookies. When you sign in, your browser keeps a login token in local storage so you
    stay signed in. Signing out removes it.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to see, correct or delete your account and anything you submitted. Email
    <a href="mailto:ben@pockethost.io">ben@pockethost.io</a> from the address you registered with. We keep PocketCon
    data until the event's follow-up is done, then delete accounts that aren't needed.
  </p>
</section>
